.TH CLIPPY-PET 1 "2026" "clippy-pet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clippy-pet \- install the Clippy Pet Codex pet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clippy-pet
.RI [ install ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B clippy-pet
.BR uninstall | status | sync | path
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B clippy-pet
.B autostart
.BR enable | disable | status
.br
.B clippy-pet
.BR version | help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clippy-pet
copies the Clippy Pet Codex pet manifest and spritesheet into
.IR $CODEX_HOME/pets/clippy-pet/ ,
where the ChatGPT desktop app (Codex) and Codex CLI TUI discover custom pets.
When
.B CODEX_HOME
is unset, Codex defaults to
.IR $HOME/.codex .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Copy the pet into place (the default command).
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove the installed pet.
.TP
.B status
Report whether the pet is installed and up to date. Exit status is 0 for
up to date, 1 for not installed, 2 for outdated.
.TP
.B sync
Equivalent to \fBinstall --if-missing\fR; used by the autostart entry.
.TP
.B path
Print the resolved install directory.
.TP
.B autostart enable|disable|status
Manage an XDG autostart entry that runs \fBsync --quiet\fR at login.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-codex\-home " " \fIDIR\fR
Use \fIDIR\fR instead of \fI$CODEX_HOME\fR or \fI$HOME/.codex\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-link
Symlink the pet directory to the package's data directory instead of
copying, so it stays current automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing installation.
.TP
.B \-\-if\-missing
Only install if not already installed.
.TP
.B \-\-migrate
Remove a legacy \fI~/.codex/pets/clipster/\fR installation before installing.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress non-error output.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Report progress and errors via a desktop notification or dialog when
available (osascript, notify-send, zenity, kdialog, or a D-Bus call).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CODEX_HOME
Overrides the Codex configuration directory.
.TP
.B CLIPPY_PET_DATA
Overrides the directory containing pet.json and spritesheet.webp.
.SH FILES
.I $CODEX_HOME/pets/clippy-pet/pet.json
.br
.I $CODEX_HOME/pets/clippy-pet/spritesheet.webp
.SH SEE ALSO
Project homepage: https://github.com/adammatthewsteinberger/clippy-pet
